  "name": "Question 4",
  "problem": "Arranged in **ascending order** and rounded to **the nearest integer**, the solutions of the equation $\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x=0.7$ for $-{180}^{\u2218}<x\\le {180}^{\u2218}$ are $x=${{field-1}}${}^{\u2218}$ and $x=$\n{{field-2}}${}^{\u2218}.$",
  "worked_solution": "First, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=\\operatorname{arccos}\u2061(0.7)=(45.572\\,9\u2026)^{\u2218}\u2248{45.573}^{\u2218}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince ${45.573}^{\u2218}$ lies inside the required domain, our first solution, rounded to the nearest integer, is $x={46}^{\u2218}.$\n\nOur first solution lies in the first quadrant and has a reference angle of \n${\\theta }_{R}={45.573}^{\u2218}.$\nSince $\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x>0,$ the second solution must lie in the fourth quadrant, and it also has a reference angle ${\\theta }_{R}={45.573}^{\u2218}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005103/assets/3ff8bb94afda0843fa6f22802ae70ca98d7e6856e8be2911ab1cb3ea2cccd2c1.png)\n\nA second solution $X$ lies in the $4$th quadrant, and we can find it using the reference angle, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & ={360}^{\u2218}-{\\theta }_{R} \\\\  & ={360}^{\u2218}-{45.573}^{\u2218} \\\\  & ={314.427}^{\u2218}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHowever, this value is not in the required domain. To get a second solution that's within the required domain, we simply subtract ${360}^{\u2218}$ from $X:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =X-{360}^{\u2218} \\\\  & ={314.427}^{\u2218}-{360}^{\u2218} \\\\  & =-{45.573}^{\u2218} \\\\  & \u2248-{46}^{\u2218}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, arranged in ascending order, the solutions are $x={-46}^{\u2218}$ and $x={46}^{\u2218}.$",
